  "settings.db_journal_label": "Journal mode:",
  "settings.db_journal_hint": "SQLite journal mode for retro-amp.db:\n\n• DELETE: Default, safe for Dropbox/OneDrive (recommended).\n• WAL: Faster for parallel access, creates .wal/.shm sidecars.\n• TRUNCATE / PERSIST: Journal file is not deleted.\n• MEMORY: Journal in RAM, fast, but data loss on crash.\n• OFF: No rollback protection — not recommended.\n\nThe change takes effect on the next restart of retro-amp.",
  "settings.tab_history": "History",
  "settings.history_enable_label": "Tracking:",
  "settings.history_enable_checkbox": "Remember tracks that start playing",
  "settings.history_limit_label": "Max. entries:",
  "settings.history_clear_button": "Clear history now",
  "settings.history_hint": "Records every started track with a timestamp in the DB.\nThe history tab groups entries by Today, Yesterday, This week\nand Older. When tracking is off, the tab stays visible but only\nshows a hint.\n\nOlder entries are pruned automatically once the limit is\nexceeded.",
  "settings.history_cleared": "History cleared ({count} entries)",
  "settings.cover_graphics_label": "Rendering mode:",
  "settings.cover_graphics_checkbox": "Use terminal graphics protocol (pixel-perfect covers)",
  "settings.cover_graphics_hint": "Uses the best available graphics protocol for pixel-perfect covers:\n\n• TGP (Kitty protocol): Kitty, WezTerm, Ghostty, Konsole\n• Sixel: Windows Terminal 1.22+, mintty, foot, xterm, iTerm2\n\nOn unsupported terminals we automatically fall back to the\nprevious Unicode half-block rendering.\n\nThe change takes effect on the next restart of the player.",
  "settings.cover_graphics_credit": "♥ Thanks to [link=\"https://github.com/lnqs/textual-image\"]lnqs/textual-image[/link] for the TGP and Sixel widgets.",
  "settings.tab_visualizer": "Visualizer",
  "settings.visualizer_mode_label": "Mode:",
  "settings.visualizer_mode_hint": "Display style of the spectrum visualizer in the transport bar:\n\n• Bars: 32-band spectrum with rainbow colors and peak-hold (default).\n• Blocks: 16 bars in Winamp style — green/yellow/red per row + peak markers.\n• Scope: spectral curve made of dots per band (smoothed).\n• Matrix: binary digits 0/1, color based on band intensity (cliamp-inspired).\n• LCD: 2 horizontal segment VU meters (bass + treble) — cassette deck look.\n\nChanges apply immediately.",
